WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.430
- I got asked out on the job twice,

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:04.266
and it was just a little bit awkward.

00:00:04.266 --> 00:00:06.770
- Shoulda said "Yeah,"
coulda got an extra tip.

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:14.650
- Never have I ever eaten
a customer's leftovers.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:16.403
- For sure.

00:00:16.403 --> 00:00:17.850
- Ooh 100%.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:21.958
- I have not.
- Everyone has.

00:00:21.958 --> 00:00:22.791
- I've wanted to.

00:00:22.791 --> 00:00:24.690
- Pretend to, like,
push it in the garbage,

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.480
and just like, sneak a
couple popcorn shrimp.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.260
- I've even hit a cup of
someone's wine before,

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.834
once or twice, come and
bring it to the dish area.

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:33.090
Look around for a little
bit, do a quick uh.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:33.923
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:33.923 --> 00:00:34.930
Then you're back on the floor.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.170
- Makes the job easier.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:37.980
- Then you gotta look
at the customers, too,

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.280
and be like "Would I make out with them?"

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.070
And that's a good
judgment of whether or not

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:42.990
I'm gonna eat their food.

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:43.880
- If it's there, I'm eating it.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:47.330
- Never have I ever dropped
food but still served it.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.143
- Not on the floor
- Ooh.

00:00:52.143 --> 00:00:53.920
- I mean, I've dropped a
couple pepperonis before

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.800
at a pizza restaurant I
worked at, on the floor,

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.310
before it was cooked, and
just picked it back up,

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:00.630
threw it on the thing,
and right back in the oven

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:02.562
- I think that's fine,
the oven kills the germs.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.020
- I was gonna say, right?

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.500
- I've done it on the
bench next to the plate.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:07.386
I don't know if that counts.

00:01:07.386 --> 00:01:08.710
- Okay.
- Probably fine.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.120
- Yeah I dropped it on the floor.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.360
- It wasn't like a big
deal, you know what I mean?

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.010
It wasn't like on a very
dirty ground or anything.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.390
- I've definitely dropped food before,

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:17.490
and thought about serving it,

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:21.410
but I just seized the
opportunity to eat it myself.

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:23.080
- Oh they were so mean.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.160
The customers were so mean,

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:28.270
and it dropped on the floor
for like three seconds

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:30.720
and I picked it up and
looked at my coworker

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.500
and he was like "I didn't see anything"

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.310
and I was like "Okay."

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:37.440
- Never have I ever spat
in a customer's food.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:38.392
- Definitely not.
- I have not.

00:01:38.392 --> 00:01:39.300
- I would never do that.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.094
- I've seen it in movies
and it's too much for me.

00:01:41.094 --> 00:01:42.006
- No, it's gross.

00:01:42.006 --> 00:01:42.840
- Definitely have not.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.340
- Again, but like, really wanted to.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:46.760
When they're just so rude.

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:48.690
- Oh my God, you have?

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:49.570
- They deserved it.

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:52.930
This lady, she ordered very specifically,

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:55.400
and I got her order 100% right.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.720
She wanted to complain about it,

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.200
'cause she wanted her meal for free.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.280
I said, "Ma'am, I wrote
everything down word for word."

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:04.710
She called me a derogatory
name, about my race,

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:07.270
and threw her ice at me.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:10.480
So, when she got her
correct food this time,

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:12.510
it was a little bit extra correct.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:14.350
- That's fair then, if they
call you a name, I get that.

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:16.270
- They came at me, they
threw their drink at me so.

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:17.103
- Oh my God.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.330
- What'd you expect?

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:20.360
- Never have I ever lied
about knowing if a dish

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:23.920
had gluten or some other
product in it or not.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:26.120
- I was still in training and she asked

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.140
if the soup was vegan,
and it was tomato soup,

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.040
so I took a chance and was
like "Yeah, it's whatever."

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:32.873
It's not.

00:02:32.873 --> 00:02:35.760
The stock in the soup is
actually chicken stock,

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.460
and it's tomato bisque,
which is 90% cream.

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:40.909
I learned my lesson from that.

00:02:40.909 --> 00:02:42.270
- Anything bad happen?
- She's still alive.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:44.880
- I feel like most people
don't even know what gluten is,

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.730
so when they it to me,
I'm like "I don't know."

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.410
And they ask me if it
has gluten, it's like,

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:51.100
"Shouldn't you know if a
potato has gluten in it?"

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:51.933
I don't know.

00:02:51.933 --> 00:02:55.360
- I have when I was more
ignorant about those things.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.170
'Cause I started working
in the restaurant business

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:59.100
when I was like 16, so I
remember the first time

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:01.488
I got asked that question and I was like,

00:03:01.488 --> 00:03:02.960
"I don't know, no there's not."

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.950
But then I had a friend
whose mom had Celiac disease

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.580
and I very quickly learned,
like, the seriousness of it

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.130
and I was like, okay lesson learned,

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:12.310
I will always triple check ingredients.

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:14.010
- Never have I ever given bad service

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:16.510
because I thought they wouldn't tip well.

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:17.620
- I've never given bad service

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:18.453
because I didn't think anybody

00:03:18.453 --> 00:03:20.580
was going to be a bad tipper, but I mean,

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:22.730
there's obviously been
times where, you know,

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:25.210
your soul's just not
into it, because you know

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.255
they're not going to give you any money.

00:03:26.255 --> 00:03:27.088
- I don't know.

00:03:27.088 --> 00:03:27.921
- Oh be honest.

00:03:27.921 --> 00:03:31.560
- I may have, but I also haven't
because this happens to me

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:32.760
because I'm foreign.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:35.010
I've noticed that servers
will be really rude to me

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.263
from the start, sometimes.

00:03:36.263 --> 00:03:37.130
- 'Cause they think, yeah.

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:38.900
- 'Cause they're like, she's
foreign, she's not gonna tip.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:41.320
I'm like, actually I'm
probably gonna tip better

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.410
than everyone else.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:43.260
- Yeah.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.534
- And I'm always right.

00:03:44.534 --> 00:03:45.370
- Yes
- I'm always right.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:48.050
- Never have I ever messed
up an order on purpose.

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:49.100
- What would the purpose be?

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.090
- Yeah, that's what I'm thinking.

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:51.470
What would the purpose of that be?

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:53.170
That's just gonna cause hell.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:54.794
- Yeah I don't think I have.

00:03:54.794 --> 00:03:56.880
- No, definitely a lot by mistake.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:57.713
- Oh.

00:03:57.713 --> 00:03:58.546
- I've never messed it up on purpose.

00:03:58.546 --> 00:04:01.140
I think the mistakes come
from just kind of zoning out

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.070
and not being focused enough.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:05.410
- I have definitely messed
up an order on purpose

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.720
because I felt the person
was like a mean-ass (bleep).

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:08.790
And I thought it was just funny, like,

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.390
someone had a lot of
allergies, supposedly,

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:13.910
like they were gluten free,
they were flour free, I mean,

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:14.860
I worked at a pizza restaurant.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:16.500
They ended up doing the order wrong,

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:17.540
and just kept bringing it back.

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:18.373
It made me laugh.

00:04:18.373 --> 00:04:20.420
- Never have I ever dated a customer.

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:21.831
- Huh?

00:04:21.831 --> 00:04:24.090
I've got to think about that one.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:25.740
I'm going to go with the safe answer here.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:26.600
- I have not.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.189
I wish I would have.

00:04:28.189 --> 00:04:29.022
- No.

00:04:29.022 --> 00:04:29.855
- I have not.

00:04:29.855 --> 00:04:31.590
- Yeah I have.
- I've had a lot of, have you?

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:33.240
- Yeah, I've worked in bars.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.370
- Okay, see I've never worked in bars

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:38.640
so it was always just breakfast food.

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.370
So the type of people
that were asking me out

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:42.190
were like 50 year olds.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:44.980
- Yeah I've definitely gone out for drinks

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:46.690
with cute guys I've met.

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:47.523
- Hell yeah.

00:04:47.523 --> 00:04:49.510
- Never have I ever had sex at work.

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:51.810
- That'd be rather tough.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:52.643
- Ooh.

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:55.780
- I haven't, but I know people that have.

00:04:57.012 --> 00:04:57.845
- I have.

00:04:58.811 --> 00:05:00.930
I never thought I would admit that.

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:04.060
It was with an old co-worker,
there was no one around,

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:05.830
if that makes up for it.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:08.423
- [Camera Man] Was it
in the walk-in freezer?

00:05:08.423 --> 00:05:10.240
- No, not in the freezer.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:12.120
- I'm kind of disappointed
for this, I feel like.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.860
- I know, I really wish
I could flip it around,

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:14.980
I really do.
- Right?

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.670
- It's an interesting industry to be in.

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.870
It sucks sometimes,
sometimes its wonderful.

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:19.830
I don't want to be cliche,

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:22.120
but sometimes I like to see
the smiles on people's faces.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:24.830
There are happy people when
you're working in this industry.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:26.210
Sometimes, sometimes.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.070
- There are definitely
really interesting stories

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:30.770
that can come from customers
who are just a little bit off

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:32.010
or super rude to you.

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:33.680
- You should always be
nice to your servers,

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.420
like, they're taking care of your food,

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:36.710
they're working so hard.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:37.543
- They have power.

00:05:37.543 --> 00:05:39.020
- They're also taking
care of six other tables

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:39.853
at the same time.

00:05:39.853 --> 00:05:40.686
- Sometimes more.

00:05:40.686 --> 00:05:42.930
- Regardless of how much I hated working,

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:45.550
and still hate working in
the restaurant industry,

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:46.410
it's actually kind of fun

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:48.010
and there's a lot of good
stories you can tell.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:50.810
- I feel like we have
the same general answers

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:52.910
to the questions so no matter
what kind of restaurant

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.708
you work at it, I feel like
it's all kind of the same.

00:05:54.708 --> 00:05:57.291
(upbeat music)

